WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.711
Stage five: the owner's tour.

2
00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:09.126
The dashboard is one command: dashboard.sh.

3
00:00:09.226 --> 00:00:16.729
It opens on 127.0.0.1, read-only, built from your Markdown files.

4
00:00:16.829 --> 00:00:20.962
A file written by the coach shows up within thirty seconds.

5
00:00:21.812 --> 00:00:24.643
Today: do I run, ease off or rest?

6
00:00:24.743 --> 00:00:29.153
Verdict and reason, morning check, today's plan with its weather.

7
00:00:30.003 --> 00:00:32.258
Week: planned versus done.

8
00:00:32.358 --> 00:00:38.603
Tuesday's threshold is cancelled, hills slide to Thursday: rule seven explains why.

9
00:00:39.453 --> 00:00:42.882
Fitness and load: condition, fatigue, form.

10
00:00:42.982 --> 00:00:47.136
And Trail Shape: does training cover what the race will demand?

11
00:00:47.986 --> 00:00:51.415
Sessions: Sunday's run, eighteen kilometres.

12
00:00:51.515 --> 00:00:54.709
Detected climbs, then kilometre splits.

13
00:00:55.986 --> 00:00:58.945
Decisions: why did this session change?

14
00:00:59.045 --> 00:01:02.410
Each entry shows before, after and sources.

15
00:01:03.986 --> 00:01:08.311
And also: health, nutrition, reports, performance, calendar.

16
00:01:10.986 --> 00:01:13.348
It all fits on a phone too.

17
00:01:13.448 --> 00:01:17.965
Behind a reverse proxy, in Docker, the workspace stays read-only.

18
00:01:20.686 --> 00:01:24.648
To go further: the “Views” page of the documentation.
